is here so a consumer knows exactly what ends up on their link line.


Third party components this project uses
----------------------------------------

NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit: cuBLAS, cuSPARSE, cuSOLVER, the CUDA Runtime (cudart), and
NVML.
  Role: cuBLAS and cuSPARSE are the correctness oracles and the performance
  baselines every claim in this repository is measured against; cuSOLVER backs
  ckl::DenseSolver; NVML supplies the clock, temperature and throttle telemetry
  that gates whether a benchmark run is trusted.
  Posture: not redistributed here. They are installed with the CUDA Toolkit and
  linked from that installation, under the NVIDIA Software License Agreement and
  the CUDA Supplement that come with the toolkit. A binary built from this
  source and shipped onward has to satisfy NVIDIA's redistribution terms for
  whichever of these libraries it carries.
  Link: https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/

GoogleTest, version 1.17.0.
  Role: the test framework. Test only; no part of it reaches the installed
  library.
  Posture: fetched at configure time by CMake FetchContent from
  https://github.com/google/googletest, pinned to the tag v1.17.0, built inside
  the build tree and never installed. BSD 3-Clause License.


Components named in the design but not yet used
-----------------------------------------------

These appear in the plan and in the algorithm enum for ABI stability. Nothing in
release 1.1.0 links or downloads them, and this file will say so plainly on the
day that changes.

  cuFFT   (NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit, same license posture as the libraries above)
  CUB     (NVIDIA, BSD 3-Clause; ships inside the CUDA Toolkit as part of CCCL)
  CUTLASS (NVIDIA, BSD 3-Clause; would be fetched, not vendored)
